# run27 (2026-09-22 18:09-18:18 -03): nouveau HDMI output-format matrix, one driver swap, 16 steps.
# Module: /K3D/temp/k317/nouveau-hdmi-chroma-bench-experimental.ko sha256 ff94c6fbb3d0ef374ac5d8e7e20a963e02208202b3155e50252cd11b39de0a2c
#   = v2 deep-colour bench shape + the chroma series (head OCSC1/clamp/procamp, Broadcast RGB,
#     YCbCr 4:4:4/4:2:2 with joint format x depth selection; bench-only "color format" property
#     with the drm-misc-next name/values, since 7.0 lacks the core one).
# Sink: Sony KDL-46HX855 (HDMI 1.4, DC_30/DC_36/DC_Y444, YCbCr 4:4:4+4:2:2, 225 MHz, QS=0), GA106.
# Result, owner-verbatim: "FULL SUCCESS! RGB - 8/10/12, auto, limited and full all pass with full
#   colors (on each limit, of course). YUV 444 - 12/10/8 pass with full colors. YUV 422 12/10/8 pass
#   with full colors. SBS YUV 444 12-bit - pass with full colors (text is flickering in 3D, but it's
#   ok - something in the render code might be making the text background act ackwards). TAB Limited
#   12-bit pass with full colors. FP YUV 422 12-bit - pass with full colors."
# Driver selection per step is in the "driver:" lines (first line of a step may be the property
# commit on the console mode; the step's own modeset follows).
# Post-run review of this log (Opus): (1) the FP step's selection line reports rate=74250 kHz -- the
#   selection and SCDC gate used the per-eye mode clock, while the head runs the frame-packed
#   crtc_clock (148.5 MHz here). Harmless on this 225 MHz sink, wrong in general; fixed in the
#   series (nv50_hdmi_char_rate, folded into v2 patches 1/2) and in the bench module (-v2).
#   (2) all steps were HD, so the BT.601 matrix path never ran; (3) the 3D label flicker was the
#   tool repainting the label rows every frame. (2)+(3)+(1) re-verified by harness mode chroma2.
